 string literals, which works (Character is ExpressibleByStringLiteral).

Edge case: if `#` is followed by a non-word character, j == start, so we skip and
 advance i to j (== start, i.e., the character immediately after `#`). Good — avoids
 infinite loop.

This preserves order.

